is given, names it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"iOS, tvOS, watchOS, and visionOS offer no public API for a process to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"read its own entitlements, so there the build is trusted unless you pass","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isEntitled"},{"text":". That trust is narrower than it sounds: those platforms","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refuse to launch a binary claiming entitlements its profile doesn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"grant, so a running build lacks CloudKit only if its entitlements file","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never asked for it — a fact fixed at build time, which surfaces on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".iCloud"},{"text":" probe in development. A build that is entitled but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pointed at the wrong container is still caught, from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CKError.badContainer"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".missingEntitlement"},{"text":" the account probe gets.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/SyncPreflightService\/live(containerID:isEntitled:)"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync","doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/SyncPreflightService"]]},"references":{"doc://SwiduxCloudKitSync/documentation/SwiduxCloudKitSync":{"title":"SwiduxCloudKitSync","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxcloudkitsync","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://Swi